@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@*
    The shell-less layout for the auth family (page archetype "Auth card").
    The design system's own catalogue marks this archetype "forms (no shell)",
    and it is the only archetype that says so: signing in is the one thing you
    do before you have anywhere to navigate to, and a sidebar full of tools you
    cannot open yet is furniture that asks to be clicked.

    What it gives up, deliberately: the top bar's theme switch. The theme still
    applies — App.razor stamps data-theme on <html> from the aldt-theme cookie
    before Blazor starts — it just cannot be changed from here. Somebody who is
    not signed in has no preference stored to change.

    #blazor-error-ui is repeated from MainLayout rather than shared: Login and
    LoginChallenge are @@rendermode InteractiveServer, so a dropped circuit on
    an auth page needs the same recovery affordance as anywhere else.
*@

<div class="auth">
    @Body
</div>

<div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
    An unhandled error has occurred.
    <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
    <span class="dismiss">×</span>
</div>
